WEBVTT

00:12.760 --> 00:15.610
<i>I didn't get a wink of sleep.</i>

00:16.420 --> 00:22.290
<i>That room was in no state for it,
 so I had her sleep in here, but...</i>

00:22.740 --> 00:25.510
<i>Seeing her look so helpless...</i>

00:25.510 --> 00:28.290
<i>It'd be impossible for
my imagination not to run wild!</i>

00:28.540 --> 00:34.510
<b>Zzz...</b>

00:28.940 --> 00:31.530
<i>Not that I have the guts 
to actually try something.</i>

00:31.530 --> 00:34.510
<i>The thought of upsetting her 
 makes that out of the question.</i>

00:34.510 --> 00:37.930
<b>Grrrr</b>

00:36.500 --> 00:37.930
Guess I'll grab something to eat.

00:55.210 --> 00:56.410
You're awake.

00:59.620 --> 01:03.660
Yes. Good morning, Master.

01:04.090 --> 01:06.470
<i>She's willing to greet me.</i>

01:08.140 --> 01:08.880
<i>Wait.</i>

01:09.240 --> 01:12.840
<i>What are you supposed to say 
when someone says good morning?</i>

01:12.840 --> 01:14.610
<i>Just say "good morning" back?</i>

01:14.610 --> 01:15.860
<i>"Hello there"?</i>

01:15.860 --> 01:18.300
<i>"Good day to you" is probably a bit much...</i>

01:23.540 --> 01:25.190
I brought food.

01:25.190 --> 01:26.270
You may eat.

01:26.840 --> 01:30.110
<i>I can't even give a proper greeting?!</i>

01:46.080 --> 01:53.050
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

03:01.990 --> 03:06.990
<b>Episode 2:
First Love With Social Anxiety
 Tastes a Lot Like Moldy Bread</b>

03:10.460 --> 03:15.420
<b>Munch
Munch</b>

03:10.970 --> 03:14.200
<i>When did I become such a failure of a person?</i>

03:14.200 --> 03:15.420
<i>Probably right from the start.</i>

03:16.260 --> 03:20.620
Um... Master, are you eating
 the same thing as me?

03:21.600 --> 03:23.010
Is that strange?

03:23.010 --> 03:24.850
No... it's just...

03:25.190 --> 03:28.660
I'm lucky to be fed at all.

03:28.660 --> 03:33.230
But it's strange that you're 
eating the same thing.

03:34.510 --> 03:35.650
Wait...

03:35.650 --> 03:38.480
<i>Is the food too plain?!</i>

03:36.690 --> 03:38.480
<b>Today's breakfast:
Jerky & Milk</b>

03:38.480 --> 03:40.730
Well... yes.

03:40.730 --> 03:43.990
It's the kind of thing that would be 
typically fed to a slave like myself.

03:43.990 --> 03:45.950
<i>So it's less food and more like...</i>

03:46.950 --> 03:49.790
<b>Feed</b>

03:47.370 --> 03:48.290
<i>Feed?</i>

03:49.790 --> 03:54.830
<i>That said, she seems more worried than angry.</i>

03:54.830 --> 03:57.600
<i>Wait, no! That look says...</i>

03:57.600 --> 04:02.130
<i>"If I don't do something about 
this guy, he's going to die!"</i>

04:02.130 --> 04:04.130
<b>Crunch crunch crunch...</b>

04:04.870 --> 04:10.140
<i>Oh, I get it. I guess this 
barely even qualifies as food.</i>

04:10.220 --> 04:15.020
<b>Munch
Munch</b>

04:10.990 --> 04:15.450
<i>I've eaten stuff like this my whole life,
 so I've never questioned it.</i>

04:15.450 --> 04:18.110
<i>Other than jerky, 
there's also been moldy bread...</i>

04:15.650 --> 04:18.110
<b>Munch
Munch</b>

04:18.760 --> 04:21.460
<i>There's something nostalgic 
about that sour taste.</i>

04:22.110 --> 04:25.220
I wonder what normal people eat.

04:27.740 --> 04:31.870
This might be presumptuous,
 but should I prepare something?!

04:33.080 --> 04:34.210
<b>Twitch</b>

04:35.070 --> 04:37.450
You can cook?

04:37.450 --> 04:39.210
It's mostly just imitation, but...

04:39.540 --> 04:41.590
<i>Home cooking?!</i>

04:43.170 --> 04:47.620
<i>My dedication to sorcery has kept me 
from even considering the possibility...</i>

04:47.620 --> 04:51.640
<i>And now the girl I'm in love with 
is going to cook for me?!</i>

04:53.810 --> 04:57.020
Nephy! It seems our task is clear.

04:57.020 --> 04:57.860
Right.

04:59.810 --> 05:01.600
We're going grocery shopping in town!

05:03.190 --> 05:04.530
Need a ride?

05:04.530 --> 05:07.450
The price for the two of you 
will be three bronze pieces.

05:07.800 --> 05:10.700
<i>Oh, right. I have no money!</i>

05:11.160 --> 05:12.200
One million!

05:12.840 --> 05:15.260
One million gold Kuriotes.

05:15.260 --> 05:18.920
<i>One million... One million...</i>

05:19.530 --> 05:22.350
Walking every now and then isn't so bad.

05:22.350 --> 05:23.050
It's not?

05:28.610 --> 05:31.060
<i>I need to shore up my finances somehow.</i>

05:31.450 --> 05:34.310
<i>I don't have a single bronze 
coin left at the castle.</i>

05:34.310 --> 05:37.560
<i>I might be able to sell the torture 
equipment that's left there, but...</i>

05:37.560 --> 05:40.060
<i>I don't have the money to 
hire someone to pack it up!</i>

05:40.460 --> 05:44.320
<i>Should I have mugged the coach driver?</i>

05:47.630 --> 05:53.060
<i>No! There's no telling what she'd think of 
someone who'd resort to that.</i>

05:53.060 --> 05:56.040
<i>I get the feeling it'd be bad! 
Maybe I should...</i>

05:56.040 --> 06:00.040
<b>Elven Home
Kitchen</b>

05:56.040 --> 06:00.040
<b>Bodyguard</b>

05:56.350 --> 06:00.040
<i>Just get rid of the castle and 
open up a diner with Nephy?</i>

06:03.630 --> 06:05.250
Hold it!

06:05.250 --> 06:06.380
Leave your goods behind!

06:07.720 --> 06:08.970
No!

06:09.260 --> 06:10.480
Master!

06:11.190 --> 06:14.010
Oh, must be a robbery or something.

06:15.650 --> 06:20.480
They're not sorcerers or anything. 
Just a band of harmless robbers.

06:25.730 --> 06:27.010
What's wrong?

06:27.010 --> 06:27.950
Nothing...

06:30.840 --> 06:31.820
<i>Wait...</i>

06:32.650 --> 06:35.290
<i>Was this how Nephy was kidnapped, too?!</i>

06:37.160 --> 06:39.530
Nephy, watch closely.

06:42.710 --> 06:44.920
It's like brushing some dust away.

06:44.920 --> 06:46.400
A sorcerer!

06:46.400 --> 06:48.710
A sorcerer?! Why?!

06:48.710 --> 06:52.440
Settle down! Sorcerers need to rest 
before casting another spell!

06:52.440 --> 06:53.850
Get him before he does!

06:55.500 --> 06:57.860
Nephy, stay behind me.

06:59.280 --> 07:03.310
<i>I'm not going to say anything as 
 self-serving as "I'm going to protect you."</i>

07:03.960 --> 07:07.320
<i>But I'll demonstrate that you have
 nothing to fear from them.</i>

07:07.320 --> 07:09.110
Die!

07:11.990 --> 07:13.370
I-It can't be!

07:13.670 --> 07:18.370
Yeah, I can't believe you'd try and take 
on a sorcerer with brute strength, either.

07:24.730 --> 07:26.240
Boss!

07:26.240 --> 07:29.630
Sir! Sir, you've gotta help us!

07:30.750 --> 07:32.840
A sorcerer, helping others...

07:33.460 --> 07:34.930
What an odd sight.

07:35.290 --> 07:37.640
I take it they hired you?

07:37.640 --> 07:39.700
It's part of our arrangement.

07:39.700 --> 07:45.150
I don't know who you are, 
but you'll regret crossing my path.

07:53.240 --> 07:58.170
I see. Using the flames to 
trace another casting circle...

07:58.170 --> 08:00.870
I don't really see any reason 
to sit back and wait, though.

08:03.790 --> 08:06.850
Not bad! But a step too slow!

08:06.850 --> 08:07.880
Now, turn to cinders!

08:13.280 --> 08:16.260
Wh-What the?! Why can't I cast the spell?!

08:17.970 --> 08:21.570
I've usurped control of your casting circle.

08:21.570 --> 08:24.690
It no longer belongs to you.

08:34.700 --> 08:37.040
What's wrong? Come at me.

08:37.040 --> 08:40.660
If you were willing to steal from others, 
you must be ready to be stolen from.

08:50.250 --> 08:53.090
<i>Huh? Did I mess up again?</i>

08:54.560 --> 09:00.030
Now, as you can see, Nephy, 
robbers like that are as harmless as dust.

09:00.030 --> 09:02.180
Brush them aside, and they'll settle down.

09:02.740 --> 09:06.650
Are they really harmless,
 considering they attacked the coach?

09:12.430 --> 09:15.590
Well, damn, Mister Sorcerer! You saved us!

09:15.590 --> 09:17.910
I guess there are good sorcerers, too!

09:17.910 --> 09:23.330
Listen, Mister, would it be okay 
if you rode with us for protection?

09:23.330 --> 09:25.030
I'll be sure to pay you.

09:25.030 --> 09:26.420
S-Sure.

09:28.060 --> 09:29.670
<i>What is happening?</i>

09:29.670 --> 09:32.710
<i>Does money really come along this easily?</i>

09:33.040 --> 09:37.910
<i>If I go around running off bad guys,
people will just pay me for it?</i>

09:39.120 --> 09:43.700
<i>Wait, no. Sorcerers are usually the 
bad guys who are being hunted.</i>

09:43.700 --> 09:45.520
<i>That means me.</i>

09:45.520 --> 09:50.310
<i>Still, I've scattered my fair 
share of annoying robbers,</i>

09:50.310 --> 09:53.230
<i>but I've never been thanked for it before.</i>

09:54.160 --> 09:57.470
You work for him, right? 
What a beautiful gal!

09:57.470 --> 09:59.110
You have a wonderful master.

09:59.110 --> 10:03.370
<i>Are they unafraid because Nephy is with me?</i>

10:04.690 --> 10:06.140
Master...

10:06.140 --> 10:06.870
What is it?

10:07.300 --> 10:11.000
Why did you save these people?

10:11.000 --> 10:14.250
Well, I guess that was an
 unintended consequence.

10:14.760 --> 10:19.760
I just wanted to show that you had 
nothing to fear from those robbers.

10:20.060 --> 10:23.640
<i>But maybe this is my 
chance to catch her eye?!</i>

10:24.420 --> 10:28.320
<i>If I can say something smooth 
that'll get her to open up...</i>

10:25.270 --> 10:28.890
<b>I did it to protect you, Nephy.</b>

10:26.430 --> 10:28.890
<b>I can't abandon the weak when they're in need.</b>

10:30.900 --> 10:35.150
All I did was teach some self-important 
filth their place in the world.

10:40.530 --> 10:44.030
<i>Seriously, why do I always 
say stuff like that?</i>

10:48.040 --> 10:53.040
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

10:56.510 --> 11:00.180
<i>Now, we're here for groceries,</i>

11:00.180 --> 11:03.720
<i>but first let's take care of any 
daily necessities Nephy might need.</i>

11:04.390 --> 11:08.230
<i>What exactly does a girl need, anyway?</i>

11:08.550 --> 11:11.340
Nephy. Pick out anything you need.

11:11.340 --> 11:14.730
I'll be satisfied with any old thing 
you might have laying around.

11:14.730 --> 11:16.230
<b>Fin</b>

11:16.610 --> 11:18.300
<i>That makes sense.</i>

11:18.300 --> 11:20.590
<i>A girl who doubts her own survival</i>

11:20.590 --> 11:23.120
<i>probably doesn't have much 
in the way of material wants.</i>

11:30.790 --> 11:32.640
Welcome!

11:32.640 --> 11:37.130
What manner of clothing can 
I help you with, Mister Sorcerer?

11:37.130 --> 11:39.590
<i>She's clearly not happy to see me.</i>

11:40.680 --> 11:43.840
Put together some kind 
of outfit for this girl.

11:44.990 --> 11:46.850
What a beautiful girl!

11:53.020 --> 11:56.670
In that case, leave it to Manuela!

11:56.670 --> 11:58.420
One customer, coming through!

11:58.420 --> 11:59.530
Master!

11:59.530 --> 12:01.360
Hurry along, now!

12:02.110 --> 12:05.370
<i>That collar really does attract attention.</i>

12:05.970 --> 12:08.140
The collar must keep her mana contained.

12:08.140 --> 12:12.660
She's likely to run off without it,
 so please, be careful.

12:16.090 --> 12:18.500
How does this ensemble strike you?

12:19.000 --> 12:19.760
Right...

12:20.480 --> 12:21.210
Wha—

12:29.240 --> 12:32.510
What do you think?! I don't mind 
saying I think it's perfect!

12:32.510 --> 12:33.830
How, exactly?!

12:33.830 --> 12:36.400
How did you go from
 "some kind of outfit" to all this?!

12:37.770 --> 12:41.530
I was trying to cater to your tastes, sir.

12:41.530 --> 12:44.030
<i>Who exactly does she think I am?!</i>

12:46.900 --> 12:50.620
P-Please... don't look at me...

12:50.620 --> 12:52.460
Some normal clothing, please!

12:52.460 --> 12:55.620
But it suits her so well.

12:55.620 --> 12:57.960
In that case, let's try the next one!

12:57.960 --> 13:00.210
And drop that thing in your hands!

13:01.260 --> 13:03.090
Just a little joke, that's all!

13:09.180 --> 13:11.330
Now, what do you think of this one?

13:12.380 --> 13:14.640
It's an orthodox maid outfit,

13:14.640 --> 13:18.150
but the dress and apron are 
both made of high quality silk.

13:18.150 --> 13:20.780
The boots have healing 
sorcery applied to them,

13:20.780 --> 13:23.540
which limits the amount of exhaustion 
caused from working on your feet.

13:25.060 --> 13:26.780
What do you think, Nephy?

13:26.780 --> 13:29.070
I'll accept whatever's offered.

13:29.070 --> 13:33.860
If you keep that up, she's likely to put 
you in another getup like that one before.

13:33.860 --> 13:34.680
<b>Glint</b>

13:33.860 --> 13:34.680
Glint!

13:34.680 --> 13:36.960
I like this outfit, Master!

13:36.960 --> 13:39.820
Thanks for shopping with us!

13:44.010 --> 13:47.470
It's great that you have a 
master who cares for you.

13:49.420 --> 13:52.510
<i>He... cares for me?</i>

13:56.240 --> 13:58.530
Nephy, we'll go into that shop next.

13:58.530 --> 13:59.830
O-Okay.

14:00.440 --> 14:03.780
H-How might be of service, Mister Sorcerer?

14:04.160 --> 14:06.280
There's something I want 
you to take a look at.

14:07.380 --> 14:09.760
Do you know how to remove this collar?

14:10.860 --> 14:12.160
But...

14:12.160 --> 14:17.210
As long as you wear it, it's like you're 
still Archdemon Marchosias' property.

14:17.550 --> 14:19.210
You don't need it anymore.

14:20.700 --> 14:21.670
Right.

14:22.040 --> 14:23.000
Indeed.

14:23.290 --> 14:25.640
<i>"Indeed," my ass!</i>

14:25.640 --> 14:28.660
<i>I talked about her like she 
was an object again.</i>

14:26.170 --> 14:28.170
<i><b>Sulk</b></i>

14:30.600 --> 14:34.650
Mister Sorcerer, this thing's ensorcelled!

14:34.650 --> 14:37.100
That's too much for folks like us!

14:37.820 --> 14:41.350
And I hate to break it to you, but...

14:41.350 --> 14:44.540
I'm pretty sure the collar's trapped!

14:44.540 --> 14:47.820
If you don't remove it the right way,
 it might take her head off.

14:47.820 --> 14:50.360
<i>That rules out removing it by force.</i>

14:50.670 --> 14:54.280
Using the original key would be best.

14:54.710 --> 14:58.730
<i>No one at the auction had a key.</i>

14:58.730 --> 15:01.410
<i>It's likely somewhere inside 
of Marchosias' castle.</i>

15:02.390 --> 15:04.340
I appreciate it. You can have this.

15:04.340 --> 15:07.380
C'mon, sir, I haven't done 
anything to earn that!

15:07.850 --> 15:11.340
Not to mention, I couldn't 
accept payment from you!

15:13.300 --> 15:17.540
You saved me, once before.

15:17.540 --> 15:20.020
It was about a year ago...

15:20.500 --> 15:25.520
When my coach was under attack, 
you saved my daughter and me.

15:25.870 --> 15:28.280
We ran off because we were scared,

15:28.280 --> 15:31.240
but you were nice enough to let us go.

15:32.420 --> 15:34.530
I hope you can forgive us!

15:34.840 --> 15:37.870
<i>Out of the countless pests I've swatted,</i>

15:37.870 --> 15:40.460
<i>some of them must've been 
attacking this blacksmith.</i>

15:40.940 --> 15:44.930
I'll take this back, then, but you don't 
need to worry about that meaningless act.

15:44.930 --> 15:46.250
I don't even remember it.

15:46.660 --> 15:48.810
Well, I'll never forget!

15:48.810 --> 15:51.260
If you ever need anything, 
by all means, let me know!

15:53.760 --> 15:55.970
<i>What's going on today?!</i>

15:55.970 --> 15:59.760
<i>People are being so friendly 
it's creeping me out!</i>

15:59.760 --> 16:02.730
<i>Having Nephy around makes 
this big a difference?!</i>

16:03.210 --> 16:07.070
He was too scary to even speak to before.

16:07.620 --> 16:09.940
But look at him now.

16:16.450 --> 16:18.950
<i>The sun's already setting.</i>

16:18.950 --> 16:23.170
<i>I shouldn't make Nephy cook 
after getting home so late.</i>

16:30.910 --> 16:31.810
Um...

16:33.040 --> 16:37.420
Master, do you intend to remove this collar?

16:37.420 --> 16:38.820
That's the plan.

16:39.620 --> 16:44.140
Do you not think I'll run away once it's gone?

16:44.650 --> 16:47.810
<i>Well... the idea doesn't thrill me.</i>

16:47.810 --> 16:50.140
<i>And it's pretty likely to happen.</i>

16:50.140 --> 16:54.820
<i>Nephy has no reason to be 
invested in me as I am in her.</i>

16:54.820 --> 16:58.830
<i>But even then...
 Even if it means she might run...</i>

16:59.150 --> 17:01.850
It's not as if I can take 
it off right now, anyway.

17:01.850 --> 17:03.460
I wouldn't get your hopes up.

17:03.780 --> 17:07.880
<i>Why couldn't I just say,
 "But I still want to take it off you"?!</i>

17:08.530 --> 17:09.340
Right.

17:12.120 --> 17:16.850
<i>Maybe there's a sorcerous tome with 
lessons on how to talk to girls.</i>

17:13.840 --> 17:17.800
<b>Stare</b>

17:18.260 --> 17:22.000
What's wrong? Do you not know 
how to use a knife and fork?

17:22.000 --> 17:22.810
No...

17:28.290 --> 17:32.190
I've just... never eaten like this before.

17:32.550 --> 17:34.150
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

17:34.560 --> 17:37.650
<i>I think I finally understand 
what it is about Nephy</i>

17:37.650 --> 17:39.990
<i>that grabbed my attention at a glance.</i>

17:39.990 --> 17:41.770
<i>We're the same.</i>

17:41.770 --> 17:43.960
<i>She's just like I was when I had no power,</i>

17:43.960 --> 17:47.120
<i>despairing at a world
where I didn't belong...</i>

17:47.510 --> 17:49.830
Just start with whatever 
you think looks best.

17:50.370 --> 17:54.140
There's no one here you 
need to show restraint for.

17:54.140 --> 17:54.840
But...

17:54.840 --> 17:59.430
Just eat. It should be much better 
than the jerky from this morning.

18:03.290 --> 18:04.550
Thank you for the food.

18:11.770 --> 18:13.780
Gasp

18:18.990 --> 18:20.030
<b>Nom</b>

18:20.030 --> 18:24.660
<b>Roll</b>

18:21.910 --> 18:23.770
You won't taste anything from licking it.

18:23.770 --> 18:24.660
You have to bite it!

18:24.660 --> 18:25.290
<b>Splch</b>

18:27.140 --> 18:28.580
W-Well?

18:27.330 --> 18:28.040
<b>Gulp</b>

18:29.050 --> 18:31.580
I think... it's good.

18:33.420 --> 18:36.670
I was expecting it to be sweeter.

18:36.670 --> 18:39.050
But it's very juicy.

18:51.940 --> 18:52.980
Here.

18:52.980 --> 18:54.980
<i>Say... what?!</i>

18:55.460 --> 18:58.900
<i>She's... going to feed me?!</i>

18:58.900 --> 19:02.400
<i>With the spoon she just 
put in her mouth, too.</i>

19:02.400 --> 19:03.580
<i>Is this allowed?!</i>

19:05.240 --> 19:07.000
<b>Munch
Munch
Munch</b>

19:07.270 --> 19:08.430
It's good.

19:08.430 --> 19:09.250
Yes.

19:10.000 --> 19:13.430
You never give me any orders, Master.

19:13.430 --> 19:15.350
I guess not.

19:15.350 --> 19:16.420
Master...

19:17.110 --> 19:22.340
Will you allow me to do things that 
I think will be of use to you?

19:23.650 --> 19:26.760
I will. Do as you wish, Nephy.

19:27.080 --> 19:29.770
Right. I will, then.

19:33.760 --> 19:35.660
You like these, right?

19:35.660 --> 19:37.070
Go ahead.

19:39.490 --> 19:40.530
<b>Nom</b>

19:40.890 --> 19:42.050
What do you think?

19:42.720 --> 19:44.530
It's good.

19:51.010 --> 19:53.050
<i>For now, it seems...</i>

19:53.050 --> 19:56.850
<i>seeing each other as master and 
servant has helped things settle down.</i>

20:08.190 --> 20:12.480
<i>That was no dream. 
Unbelievably, a sorcerer saved my life.</i>

20:13.170 --> 20:17.030
<i>We'd been exterminating wicked 
sorcerers who target young women...</i>

20:17.030 --> 20:18.480
<i>And were on the way home.</i>

20:19.130 --> 20:22.760
<i>One of the Angelic Knights 
suddenly attacked us.</i>

20:23.980 --> 20:29.190
<i>But later, I learned it was really one of the 
Facestealers, the very group we'd been after.</i>

20:30.150 --> 20:33.790
<i>And that man... his name is Zagan.</i>

20:34.060 --> 20:36.790
<i>He had a very cruel look to him.</i>

20:37.220 --> 20:41.020
<i>But something about him 
seemed... lonely, too.</i>

20:43.450 --> 20:45.290
Lost in thought?

20:45.970 --> 20:47.500
Lord Clavwell!

20:47.500 --> 20:50.160
There's no need for such formalities.

20:50.160 --> 20:53.960
You're the hero responsible for 
getting rid of the sinners

20:53.960 --> 20:55.650
behind this string of kidnappings.

20:56.020 --> 21:01.730
No... you entrusted me with Angelic Knights, 
Your Lordship, of which I lost four.

21:02.040 --> 21:04.540
That's not your fault.

21:04.540 --> 21:08.040
And you returned after 
avenging your brothers.

21:08.040 --> 21:10.200
You can be proud of that deed.

21:11.440 --> 21:12.330
Yes, sir.

21:12.620 --> 21:17.180
But this incident... is not over yet.

21:17.970 --> 21:21.000
After scouring the sorcerer's lair,

21:21.000 --> 21:24.150
we've discovered another 
culprit is behind it all.

21:24.970 --> 21:27.400
The sorcerer, Zagan.

21:27.400 --> 21:31.220
He's the one truly responsible 
for these horrid kidnappings.

21:31.220 --> 21:32.640
Wha...

21:32.640 --> 21:34.640
Might this be some kind of mistake?

21:35.350 --> 21:37.660
Sorcerers are wicked.

21:37.660 --> 21:40.320
Even if he has no connection 
to these kidnappings,

21:40.320 --> 21:43.360
he is still evil, and must face judgment.

21:45.320 --> 21:49.890
Then, Your Lordship, 
please task me with this duty.

21:49.890 --> 21:52.150
I'm pleased that you would volunteer!

21:52.150 --> 21:53.450
I leave it to you then,

21:53.910 --> 21:59.960
Maiden of the Sacred Sword, 
Angelic Knight-Captain, Chastille Lillqvist!

23:30.010 --> 23:35.010
<b>Next Time:
The Quieter They Are, the Devastatingly Scarier They Are When Mad</b>
